{"id":1025,"date":"2013-02-28T20:45:48","date_gmt":"2013-02-28T20:45:48","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/?p=1025"},"modified":"2021-06-10T12:42:41","modified_gmt":"2021-06-10T12:42:41","slug":"aims-gh-board-member-receives-us-national-medal-of-science","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/aims-gh-board-member-receives-us-national-medal-of-science\/","title":{"rendered":"AIMS-GH Board Member Receives US National Medal of Science"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>On Friday, Feb. 1, 2013, President Barack Obama awarded Dr. Sylvester James Gates, a member of the board of trustees of AIMS-Ghana and Director of the Centre for String and Particle Theory, University of Maryland, with the National Medal of Science, , during a ceremony in the East Room of the White House in Washington.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The awards are the highest honours\u2019 bestowed by the United States Government upon scientists, engineers, and inventors.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Since 2009, Dr. Gates has also served on the President\u2019s Council of Advisors on Science and Technology and the Maryland State Board of Education. He has used both appointments to advocate STEM education (science, technology, engineering and mathematics education).<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"alignleft\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/15\/2016\/09\/obama-jim1-253x300.jpg\" alt=\"obama-jim1\" class=\"wp-image-744\"\/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Additional Links<\/strong><br><a href=\"http:\/\/bigstory.ap.org\/photo\/barack-obama-sylvester-james-gates-0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">http:\/\/bigstory.ap.org\/photo\/barack-obama-sylvester-james-gates-0<\/a><br><a href=\"http:\/\/www.washingtonpost.com\/local\/umd-physics-professor-awarded-national-medal-of-science\/2013\/01\/31\/e18ccf4a-6bb9-11e2-bd36-c0fe61a205f6_story.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">http:\/\/www.washingtonpost.com\/local\/umd-physics-professor-awarded-national-medal-of-science\/2013\/01\/31\/e18ccf4a-6bb9-11e2-bd36-c0fe61a205f6_story.html<\/a><br><a href=\"http:\/\/www.whitehouse.gov\/photos-and-video\/video\/2013\/02\/01\/president-obama-honors-countrys-top-innovators-and-scientists-2011\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">http:\/\/www.whitehouse.gov\/photos-and-video\/video\/2013\/02\/01\/president-obama-honors-countrys-top-innovators-and-scientists-2011<\/a><br><a href=\"http:\/\/being.publicradio.org\/programs\/2012\/codes-for-reality\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">http:\/\/being.publicradio.org\/programs\/2012\/codes-for-reality\/<\/a><br><a href=\"http:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=ZTelSwdgG0A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">http:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=ZTelSwdgG0A<\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>On Friday, Feb. 1, 2013, President Barack Obama awarded Dr. Sylvester James Gates, a member of the board of trustees of AIMS-Ghana and Director of the Centre for String and Particle Theory, University of Maryland, with the National Medal of Science, , during a ceremony in the East Room of the White House in Washington.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":2,"featured_media":1026,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"advgb_blocks_editor_width":"","advgb_blocks_columns_visual_guide":""},"categories":[1],"tags":[],"news_types":[32],"acf":[],"author_meta":{"display_name":"rose","author_link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/author\/rose\/"},"featured_img":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2020\/09\/obama-jim2-1080x675-1-300x188.jpg","coauthors":[],"tax_additional":{"categories":{"linked":["<a href=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/category\/uncategorized\/\" class=\"advgb-post-tax-term\">Uncategorized<\/a>"],"unlinked":["<span class=\"advgb-post-tax-term\">Uncategorized<\/span>"]}},"comment_count":"0","relative_dates":{"created":"Posted 